{title: 392 - Dear Lord, We Come at Set of Sun}
{subtitle: SDA Hymnal #392 • STRACATHRO • 8.6.7.6}
{lyricist: Mary Speidel}
{composer: Charles Hutcheson}
{key: C}
{time: 4/4}
{tempo: Moderato}
{meta: hymn_number 392}
{meta: tune STRACATHRO}
{meta: meter 8.6.7.6}
{meta: category Doctrines - }

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
[C/E]Dear Lord, [G7/F]we [C/E]come [G]at [Em]set [C/E]of [G#m]sun,
[Am/E]And [G/D]at [Am]Your [Dm/F]feet [C/E]we kneel
[Dm/A]To [C/G]worship [F]You, [C/G]Creator, King,
[Am]This day, [C/G]Your [G7/F]sign and [C/E]seal.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
[C/E]Our earthly tasks [G]we [Em]lay [C/E]aside,
[Am/E]According [Dm/F]to [C/E]Your Word,
[Dm/A]To [C/G]enter [F]now [Dm]Your [C/G]holy rest,
[Am]The Sabbath [G7/F]of the [C/E]Lord.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 3}
[C/E]Sweet Sabbath rest, [Em]your [C/E]sacred [G#m]hours
[Am/E]Are [G/D]as [Am]a [Dm/F]golden [C]chain
[Dm/A]That [C/G]reaches [F]back [Dm]to [C/G]Eden's gate
[Am]And points [C/G]us [G7/F]home again.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 4}
[C/E]And when [G7/F]this [C/E]earth [G]shall [Em]be [C/E]renewed,
[Am/E]And [C/G]sin and death destroyed,
[Dm/A]Shall [C/G]all redeemed [Dm]each [C/G]Sabbath day
[Am]Still meet [C/G]to [G7/F]praise their [C/E]God.
{end_of_verse}
